pal value. Hence,\n\n$$\nx≈1.212\\,03+\\pi ≈4.353\\,62\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places. \n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to two decimal places, the solutions are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}≈1.21,\\,{x}_{2}≈4.35.\n$$" 13194139539078 17592186576411 true] [17592186304822 1074 "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =\\frac{8\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\ \\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =\\frac{8\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} \\\\ 3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =8 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{8}{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{8}{3}\\right)≈1.212\\,03\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places. \n\nTo find the other solution in the given interval, we add $\\pi $ to the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\nx≈1.212\\,03+\\pi ≈4.353\\,62\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places. \n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to two decimal places, the solutions are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}≈1.21,\\,{x}_{2}≈4.35.\n$$" 13194139539078 17592186576411 false] [17592186304825 1074 "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $$\n\\displaystyle \\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =\\frac{5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\ 2\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{